        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: پازل",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "پازل (pâzel) — \"a jigsaw puzzle\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ما شبها با هم پازل درست میکنیم. mâ shabhâ bâ ham pâzel dorost mikonim. We do jigsaws together in the evenings."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "pâzel dorost kardan — to do a jigsaw."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "pâzel is a modern loan, usually traced to English puzzle. EtymDB has no entry for it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
